# PART 5 — COMPLETE SUBSCRIPTION MODEL

This is a critical part of TaskFlow. Implement the data architecture and centralized entitlement foundation accurately.

## 5.1 Subscription ownership

One subscription belongs to one Workspace.

All members of that Workspace inherit its subscription status.

The Admin manages the subscription.

Employees cannot independently purchase or modify the Workspace subscription.

## 5.2 Free plan

The Free plan provides all existing TaskFlow features subject to the existing role permissions.

However, the following premium features must remain locked:

- Entire Status Request module.
- Status Request creation.
- Employee Status Request responses.
- Google Meet generation through TaskFlow.
- Joining premium TaskFlow-generated meetings.
- Premium meeting management.
- Premium Meet credits.

Free plan:
- No Status Request functionality.
- No ordinary Status Queries.
- No Meet generation credits.

Do not remove existing task-management functionality from the Free plan.

## 5.3 Premium plan

The Premium plan provides:

1. Complete Status Request module.
2. Admin ability to create Status Requests.
3. Employee ability to view and respond to assigned requests.
4. Admin ability to generate Google Meet links.
5. Employees can join meetings when invited.
6. Unlimited ordinary Status Queries during the active subscription period.
7. Five successful Google Meet generations per Workspace per subscription period.

The five Meet credits are shared across the entire Workspace, not assigned individually to users.

Only the Admin can consume Meet credits.

One meeting sent to multiple employees consumes one credit, not one credit per employee.

## 5.4 Subscription duration

Every Premium subscription period must last exactly 30 days.

Use:

`30 days = 2,592,000 seconds`

Use server-generated UTC timestamps.

Never rely on the browser clock to determine subscription activation or expiry.

### Initial purchase

If verified payment activation occurs at time T:

- period starts at T.
- period expires at T + 2,592,000 seconds.

### Early renewal

If the user renews before expiry:

- next period starts at the current period's expiry.
- prepaid time must not be lost.
- next period expires exactly 30 days after the next period's start.

### Late renewal

If the subscription has already expired:

- next period starts at the verified payment activation time.
- do not backdate the new subscription.

### Expiration

After expiration:

- Premium features become unavailable to Admin and Employees.
- Status Request creation and responses are blocked.
- New premium Meet generation and joining are blocked.
- Existing historical records remain accessible according to role permissions.
- Subscription history remains intact.
- Renewal restores premium access.

### Credit reset

Each new 30-day period receives five fresh Meet credits.

Unused credits do not roll over.

